      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-navigation/kg-navigation.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Reading the knowledge graph — how to find the skill you need",
      "prov:value": "It exists because the instruction to take it was written down and the route\nitself was not."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-navigation/kg-navigation.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The one fact everything else follows from",
      "prov:value": "> **`kg` is the old name for the kind and still reads.** It was renamed to\n> `cat-harness` on 2026-09-19 so the kind is named for the layer that defines\n> it, like `CatHarness` itself.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-navigation/kg-navigation.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The one fact everything else follows from",
      "prov:value": "The id was\n> `cat-harness` until 2026-09-23. `RENAMED_DIRECTORY_IDS` in\n> `schemas/kg/cat-harness.ts` still reads that id as `skills`, so an older\n> declaration keeps overriding the entry it meant.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-navigation/kg-navigation.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Tool 1 — the MCP pair",
      "prov:value": "The summary is the point: it is what lets you pick\n   without fetching. (It emitted bare identifiers until 2026-09-19, which is\n   why this sentence is emphatic rather than obvious.)\n2.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-navigation/kg-navigation.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Not everything under the path is a skill",
      "prov:value": "Reading the tree as skills put 46 non-skills into the set, at which point\n  `<bootstrap.processes:skill ref=\"viewer\"/>` resolved — to a capability probe."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-navigation/kg-navigation.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Not everything under the path is a skill",
      "prov:value": "The agent-memory nodes under `memory/` declare\n  `folio-memory/v1`. Without this rule the audit treated all 25 as skills and\n  wrote 25 bogus QA sidecars beside them."
